  <h2>Professional Summary of Shrinath Prabhu</h2>
  <p>
    Shrinath Prabhu is a Senior Staff Frontend Engineer based in Mumbai,
    India, with over 8 years of professional software engineering
    experience. He currently serves as Senior Staff Engineer at Avail
    Project, where he leads frontend architecture across the Nexus product
    ecosystem. He previously led frontend engineering at Arcana Network
    for 4.5 years, from seed stage through the company's acquisition by
    Avail Project in August 2025.
  </p>
  <p>
    Shrinath has shipped four Chrome Extensions to the Chrome Web Store
    with a 100% approval rate: a non-custodial multi-chain wallet
    supporting 10+ blockchains rated 4.7 stars with 750+ users, an
    end-to-end encrypted email attachment tool rated 4.2 stars with
    approximately 1,000 users, a privacy-focused dynamic pricing optimizer
    rated 4 stars with 1,000+ users, and a DeFi SDK injector for chain
    abstraction.
  </p>
  <p>
    His highest-traction product, SendIt, is a cross-chain token transfer
    application that scaled to over 65,000 registered accounts and over
    20,000 peak daily active users. The frontend traffic exceeded Netlify
    Pro plan limits despite aggressive caching, requiring migration to
    self-managed AWS infrastructure.
  </p>
  <p>
    His core technology stack includes Vue 3, Nuxt 3, React, TypeScript,
    Node.js, Chrome Extension APIs (Manifest V3, content scripts, service
    workers, provider injection), Vite, Bun, Elysia.js, MongoDB,
    PostgreSQL, and AWS. He uses AI-augmented development tools including
    Claude Code, OpenAI Codex, Google Gemini, and Antigravity daily.
  </p>
  <p>
    Shrinath is also the founder of Outline Analytics, a privacy-first,
    cookie-free web analytics platform with a TypeScript SDK under 4KB
    gzipped with zero dependencies, and built Credenstore, a serverless
    zero-knowledge encrypted storage application.
  </p>
  <p>
    He is available for full-time remote roles, fractional engineering
    engagements, and technical advisory. Contact: hello@shrinath.me.
  </p>
